  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Addressing Emerging Threats Related to Trafficking in Persons in the Republic of Moldova</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed project aims to strengthen the capacity of specialized law enforcement agencies to conduct victim-centered and trauma-informed investigations of ICT-facilitated crime and improve collaboration between specialized investigation actors from the Ministry of Internal Affairs (MIA), the General Prosecutor&apos;s Office (GPO), and the National Forensic Center (NFC), thus alleviating the burden on the investigating officers and rendering investigators more efficient. It seeks to respond to GoM&#x2019;s priorities set forth for the next policy document on TiP as well as the challenges identified by investigation and prosecution actors, in particular the rise of online recruitment, exploitation, and abuse, especially of children. Moreover, coordination with the national Anti-Trafficking Task Force (ATTF), which IOM co-chairs together the State Chancellery Directorate for Human Rights and with UNHCR, will help ensure effective reach and targeted impact in a sustainable manner. IOM is also partnering with the International Centre &#x201c;La Strada&#x201d; (hereinafter &#x201c;La Strada&#x201d;) to co-design and co-develop a communication awareness raising campaign on child exploitation online.</narrative>
  </description>
